# Current Evolution texture: B midtone mask

`T_PaintedCloud_Evolution_v03` now imports `T_PaintedCloud_Evolution_MidtoneB_v03.png`. The asset identity stays unchanged; the rejected `T_PaintedCloud_Midtones_v03` is not used.

R (painted shade), G (manual density support), and A (coverage) are preserved byte-for-byte from the exported current texture. B replaces the obsolete per-module evolution phase with a smooth data mask, `4 * R * (1 - R)`, strongest in the midtones and zero at black/white endpoints. This is a mask derived from the existing art, not new directional lighting data.

The merged sky material reads B at the same UV as R/G/A. `CloudMidtoneColor` tints only the positive cloud-light contribution above the sky/rear-cloud backdrop; `CloudMidtoneStrength` controls the mask weight. White or zero strength preserves the prior result. Defaults: linear RGB `(0.72, 0.86, 1.0)`, strength `0.35`. Both are instance editable in `Sky|Cloud Midtone` and sent to the displayed sky MID by `UpdateSky`.

Coverage, celestial occlusion, rear-layer colour, and time-of-day lighting remain independent of the midtone tint. Automatic density pulsing was removed in commit `4fb296f60`; rotation, flow, and manual gathering remain. Earlier README descriptions of B phase and automatic evolution are historical and superseded by this note for the current Evolution asset.

At night the foreground now shares the rear cloud's positive light contrast, including `SkyboxTint`, `SkyboxIntensity`, the visibility floor, and global tint. A dedicated Custom expression copies the rear backdrop calculation and returns its unmasked contrast; it does not copy rear coverage or rear texture shape into the front cloud. The match fades from full at solar elevation -18 degrees to zero at -6 degrees, leaving daytime and sunset unchanged. Foreground shade, B midtone tint, sky blending and coverage still apply independently.
